<section class="heros-compat">
  <div class="conteneur">
    <h1>Software compatibility</h1>
    <p class="heros-compat__definition">
      AZERTY Global works with the vast majority of software.
      Here are the rare cases where an adjustment may be needed.
    </p>
    <p class="heros-compat__perimetre">
      These conflicts concern Windows, where <kbd>AltGr</kbd> is sent as <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd></span>.
    </p>
    <p class="heros-compat__canaux" id="channels">
      <strong>Which channel do you have?</strong> On Windows, the taskbar tells you.
      An AG icon near the clock: that is the Microsoft Store app, which
      <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Caps&nbsp;Lock</kbd></span> suspends and resumes.
      AZERTY Global in the keyboard list when you click <strong>FRA</strong>: that is
      the EXE installer, and <span class="insecable"><kbd>Win</kbd>+<kbd>Space</kbd></span> switches
      to your traditional AZERTY.
    </p>
    <div class="mesure-lecture">
      <div class="carte compat-pourquoi">
        <p><strong>Why do some conflicts exist?</strong></p>
        <p>
          On Windows, <kbd>AltGr</kbd> sends <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd></span> to the system.
          Modern applications (Word, Excel, browsers) correctly tell the two apart.
          A few programs, often Java- or Electron-based, confuse them,
          which can block certain AltGr characters.
          The usual solution: disable the conflicting shortcut in the software.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="conteneur">
    <div class="mesure-lecture">
      <h2 id="applications">Applications</h2>
      <p class="texte-2">Click an application to see the conflicts and the fix.</p>

      <details class="notice" id="vscode">
        <summary>VS Code: 2 conflicts</summary>
        <div class="notice__contenu prose">
          <p>
            <strong>Fix:</strong> <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>S</kbd></span>
            to open the shortcuts, then disable the conflicting entries.
            Or add an unbound entry in <code>keybindings.json</code>.
          </p>
          <ul class="compat-liste">
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>[</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>[</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+J)</span>: Jump to Matching Bracket</li>
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>]</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>]</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+K)</span>: Jump to Matching Bracket</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="notice" id="jetbrains">
        <summary>JetBrains (IntelliJ, PyCharm, WebStorm): 7 conflicts</summary>
        <div class="notice__contenu prose">
          <p>
            <strong>Fix:</strong> Settings &gt; Keymap,
            right-click the action &gt; <em>Remove Shortcut</em>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Tip:</strong> in the IntelliJ registry
            <span class="insecable">(<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd></span> &gt; <em>Registry</em>),
            disable <code>actionSystem.force.alt.gr</code> to fix all conflicts at once.
          </p>
          <ul class="compat-liste">
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>N</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>~</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+N)</span>: Inline Refactor</li>
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>œ</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+O)</span>: Optimize Imports</li>
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>T</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>–</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+T)</span>: Surround With</li>
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>ß</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+B)</span>: Go to Implementation</li>
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>H</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>|</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+H)</span>: Call Hierarchy</li>
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>J</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>[</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+J)</span>: Surround with Live Template</li>
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>F</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>}</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+F)</span>: Extract Field</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="notice" id="photoshop">
        <summary>Adobe Photoshop: 3 conflicts</summary>
        <div class="notice__contenu prose">
          <p>
            <strong>Fix:</strong> Edit &gt; Keyboard Shortcuts
            <span class="insecable">(<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd>).</span>
          </p>
          <ul class="compat-liste">
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>æ</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+A)</span>: Select All Layers</li>
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>W</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>«</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+W)</span>: Close All</li>
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>G</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>\</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+G)</span>: Clipping Mask</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="notice" id="figma">
        <summary>Figma: 1 conflict <span class="compat-etiquette">not remappable</span></summary>
        <div class="notice__contenu prose">
          <ul class="compat-liste">
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>G</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>\</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+G)</span>: Frame Selection</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="message message--avertissement">
            <p>
              <strong class="message__titre">Figma doesn’t let you remap its shortcuts.</strong>
              Use the context menu (right-click) or temporarily switch
              to the traditional AZERTY with <span class="insecable"><kbd>Win</kbd>+<kbd>Space</kbd></span>
              (EXE installer) or <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Caps&nbsp;Lock</kbd></span>
              (Microsoft Store app).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="notice" id="discord">
        <summary>Discord: 1 conflict</summary>
        <div class="notice__contenu prose">
          <p>
            <strong>Fix:</strong> Settings &gt; Keybinds,
            disable the relevant shortcut.
          </p>
          <ul class="compat-liste">
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>æ</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+A)</span>: Return to the active voice channel</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="notice" id="slack">
        <summary>Slack: 1 conflict <span class="compat-etiquette">not remappable</span></summary>
        <div class="notice__contenu prose">
          <ul class="compat-liste">
            <li><span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>T</kbd></span> blocks <kbd>–</kbd> <span class="insecable">(AltGr+T)</span>: Comment thread (Canvas)</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="message message--avertissement">
            <p>
              <strong class="message__titre">Slack’s Canvas shortcuts can’t be remapped.</strong>
              Temporarily switch with <span class="insecable"><kbd>Win</kbd>+<kbd>Space</kbd></span>
              (EXE installer) or <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Caps&nbsp;Lock</kbd></span>
              (Microsoft Store app).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="conteneur">
    <div class="mesure-lecture compat-jeux">
      <h2 id="games">Video games</h2>

      <h3 id="console">The ² key (game console)</h3>
      <p>
        AZERTY Global replaces <kbd>²</kbd> with <kbd>@</kbd> on the key to the left of <kbd>1</kbd>.
        The impact depends on how the game detects the console key:
      </p>
      <ul class="compat-liste">
        <li>
          <strong>By scancode</strong> (physical position): the console works normally.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>By character</strong> (virtual key): the console may not open.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="message message--avertissement">
        <p>
          <strong class="message__titre compat-titre-en-ligne">Solutions:</strong> rebind the console key in the game’s INI file,
          or switch to the traditional AZERTY with <span class="insecable"><kbd>Win</kbd>+<kbd>Space</kbd></span>
          (EXE installer) or <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Caps&nbsp;Lock</kbd></span>
          (Microsoft Store app).
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3 id="smart-caps-lock">Smart Caps Lock</h3>
      <p>
        AZERTY Global’s Smart Caps Lock only affects letters.
        Games detect <strong>the key press</strong>, not the Caps&nbsp;Lock state.
      </p>

      <h3 id="anti-cheat">Anti-cheat</h3>
      <p>
        The behavior depends on the Windows channel you use. Both options remain local
        and reversible, but they don’t work the same way under the hood.
      </p>
      <div class="compat-cartes">
        <div class="carte">
          <h4>EXE installer / MSKLC</h4>
          <p>
            This channel installs a standard Windows keyboard layout, with no AZERTY Global
            application hook. It is the most neutral channel if you often play games
            protected by anti-cheat.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="carte">
          <h4>Microsoft Store app</h4>
          <p>
            The app uses a local keyboard hook to remap keystrokes after
            sign-in. What you type is never recorded or sent; the app
            doesn’t inject a DLL into games, and deliberately pauses itself on some
            anti-cheat protected games.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="prose">
        If in doubt with a competitive game, use the EXE installer or
        disable the Microsoft Store app with <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Caps&nbsp;Lock</kbd>.</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="conteneur">
    <div class="mesure-lecture">
      <h2 id="tips">Tips</h2>
      <div class="compat-cartes">
        <div class="carte">
          <h3>Switch quickly</h3>
          <p>
            <span class="insecable"><kbd>Win</kbd>+<kbd>Space</kbd></span> (EXE installer) or
            <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Caps&nbsp;Lock</kbd></span>
            (Microsoft Store app) instantly switches between AZERTY Global
            and your traditional AZERTY.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="carte">
          <h3>Disable the conflicting shortcut</h3>
          <p>
            In the software’s settings, disable or delete the <span class="insecable"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+letter</span>
            shortcut that blocks the character. Each entry above gives the path.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="carte">
          <h3>Report an issue</h3>
          <p>
            Conflict not listed?
            <a href="/en/contact">Report a conflict</a> to help the community.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

